=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283839-water-bears-riding-bugs-and-forge-goddesses-new-hundred-devils?p=1283980#post1283980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Water bear? More like what-a-bear! Am I right folks?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://gph.is/1Mq9xI8\" target=\"_blank\">Curses, I can't get this GIF of Fozzie Bear to work. &gt;.&gt;</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T13:32:21-08:00","id":1283995,"title":"","content":"Forest Striders: giant insects, apparently.<br /> <br /> Not to be confused with Tree Striders, the jungle version of Claw Striders.<br /> <br /> Inevitably will be.<br /> <br /> Ninegala's write-up is interesting, and I like the sense of how she might transform those she empowers, but I feel as though her art should look more like her description.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283839-water-bears-riding-bugs-and-forge-goddesses-new-hundred-devils?p=1283950#post1283950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If mortals can dress them in armor and field them in battle, are they really bears?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would they not be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T14:25:11-08:00","id":1284002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283839-water-bears-riding-bugs-and-forge-goddesses-new-hundred-devils?p=1283995#post1283995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forest Striders: giant insects, apparently.<br /> <br /> Not to be confused with Tree Striders, the jungle version of Claw Striders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also not to be confused with Forest <i>Walkers</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T15:37:03-08:00","id":1284023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283839-water-bears-riding-bugs-and-forge-goddesses-new-hundred-devils?p=1283995#post1283995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would they not be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because a bear is an apex predator that human beings have historically found to be infeasible to domesticate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T15:57:23-08:00","id":1284026,"title":"","content":"Something doesn't stop being a species just because they get domesticated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThe very existence of flame-throwers proves that some time, somewhere, someone said to themselves, You know, I want to set those people over there on fire, but I'm just not close enough to get the job done.\u201d George Carlin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/123-trax","name":"Trax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar123_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T16:00:54-08:00","id":1284027,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but the Inuit never formed into a massive all-conquering army, had a high priestess who could summon Jacint, or occasionally battled vikings in zeppelins either.<br /> I'm not really worried about the historicity of trained war bears in Exalted. Maybe the Bear Avatar helps.<br /> <br /> Though I don't get what this idea has to do with these water bears. It's the Haslanti who live close to the sea, not the Icewalkers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T16:20:47-08:00","id":1284029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283839-water-bears-riding-bugs-and-forge-goddesses-new-hundred-devils?p=1284023#post1284023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because a bear is an apex predator that human beings have historically found to be infeasible to domesticate.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s probably more of a symbiotic relationship thanks to the patronage of their tribe\u2019s Animal Avatar then true domestication. Probably aren\u2019t breeding them in pens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T16:23:07-08:00","id":1284031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283839-water-bears-riding-bugs-and-forge-goddesses-new-hundred-devils?p=1284027#post1284027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though I don't get what this idea has to do with these water bears. It's the Haslanti who live close to the sea, not the Icewalkers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in 3E the Ice Walkers are meant to be a broad category of peoples across the Northern iceshelf. Compare with the range of different Inuit and related Arctic peoples in reality.<br /> <br /> I seem to recall The Bull\u2019s Empire may be up in the Frost Fangs this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-31-2019, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T18:08:26-08:00","id":1284045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283839-water-bears-riding-bugs-and-forge-goddesses-new-hundred-devils?p=1284023#post1284023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because a bear is an apex predator that human beings have historically found to be infeasible to domesticate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see three things in this:<br /> <br /> One, Creation has greater or lesser degrees of magic that, in the past, writers have referred to as being able to do things like make predatory animals suitable as cavalry.<br /> <br /> Two, we've possibly had domesticated canines for longer than we've had building or farming, and they're still canines.<br /> <br /> Three, the write-up makes no reference to them being domesticated. Taming and domestication are not the same thing, and many kinds of animal that would be all but impossible to domesticate have been tamed. Elephants as beasts of burden? Almost always captured from the wild; their reproductive cycle is way too long to breed them, or even balance out their captive mortality rate. <br /> <br /> Humans have, in fact, frequently tamed predatory animals. Lions, tigers and bears (as well as various kinds of wild canine) have been utilised in circus acts and similar performance for centuries. Of course, in modern times, they're hardly ever employed for anything violent if they're intended to interact with humans, since the process of taming tends to involve curbing their predatory impulses, but again, magic.<br /> <br /> (There are other predatory animals that have been tamed for hunting purposes when that isn't particularly dangerous to humans; the ones used in falconry, for instance. Those birds need to have their eggs stolen from wild nests, and carefully raised from hatching to function usefully for hunters. They haven't been bred to something compliant and useful by default.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T18:24:35-08:00","id":1284047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283839-water-bears-riding-bugs-and-forge-goddesses-new-hundred-devils?p=1284027#post1284027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really worried about the historicity of trained war bears in Exalted. Maybe the Bear Avatar helps.</div> </div> </div> </div> The write-up kinda implies it.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T19:00:14-08:00","id":1284054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283839-water-bears-riding-bugs-and-forge-goddesses-new-hundred-devils?p=1284027#post1284027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I don't get what this idea has to do with these water bears. It's the Haslanti who live close to the sea, not the Icewalkers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some <b>Ice</b>walkers migrate across the Northern seas when they ice up; particularly the tribes around Mela's Fang.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T19:49:48-08:00","id":1284058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283839-water-bears-riding-bugs-and-forge-goddesses-new-hundred-devils?p=1283875#post1283875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, okay the Northern Ursidae is a nice trainable mount with some nice latent abilities and sweet bonusses for being in the water and yet ...<i>somehow... </i>no gills merit. A slight oversight in an otherwise strong writeup.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Armoured Terror doesn't have that either.<br /> <br /> Does any aquatic animal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T20:50:48-08:00","id":1284063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283839-water-bears-riding-bugs-and-forge-goddesses-new-hundred-devils?p=1284058#post1284058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Armoured Terror doesn't have that either.<br /> <br /> Does any aquatic animal?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The benthic knifetooth's description mentions having gills, and, in fact, so does the northern ursidae's. One could argue that the benthic knifetooth and other purely water-breathing creatures only have the 0-dot version of the Gills merit, and thus don't need to have it on their sheet. But the ursidae is explicitly capable of breathing both out of and in water, so that's the 3-dot version of Gills for sure. On the third hand, I'm not sure <i>any</i> of the creature write-ups in the Core book mention &quot;common&quot; merits that the animal would logically have, just merits that are somehow unusual or non-standard. I think the standard being used is to only list merits that are unusual or require rules, and assume that the ST can work out the fact that an ursidae can breathe underwater even without mentioning the gills merit, just like a great cat can maul you without having the Claws merit, or raiton can fly without Wings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T21:04:27-08:00","id":1284064,"title":"","content":"*breathes heavily at Ninegala\u2019s quiver*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T21:24:01-08:00","id":1284068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283839-water-bears-riding-bugs-and-forge-goddesses-new-hundred-devils?p=1284063#post1284063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The benthic knifetooth's description mentions having gills, and, in fact, so does the northern ursidae's. One could argue that the benthic knifetooth and other purely water-breathing creatures only have the 0-dot version of the Gills merit, and thus don't need to have it on their sheet. But the ursidae is explicitly capable of breathing both out of and in water, so that's the 3-dot version of Gills for sure. On the third hand, I'm not sure <i>any</i> of the creature write-ups in the Core book mention &quot;common&quot; merits that the animal would logically have, just merits that are somehow unusual or non-standard. I think the standard being used is to only list merits that are unusual or require rules, and assume that the ST can work out the fact that an ursidae can breathe underwater even without mentioning the gills merit, just like a great cat can maul you without having the Claws merit, or raiton can fly without Wings.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it doesn't explicitly say they breath both in and out of water, it says &quot;Gills in their necks allow them to dive for long periods to hunt fish that live in caves deep below the water\u2019s surface, or to evade human hunters\u2019 spears and harpoons,&quot; which reads to me like they do need to surface like whales.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T01:32:22-08:00","id":1284090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283839-water-bears-riding-bugs-and-forge-goddesses-new-hundred-devils?p=1283995#post1283995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ninegala's write-up is interesting, and I like the sense of how she might transform those she empowers, but I feel as though her art should look more like her description.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, I'd expect more Vulkan's long-lost sister from her description. The depiction of the &quot;Ur-Golem&quot; armour also feels like a potentially cool idea went to waste.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T07:15:21-08:00","id":1284127,"title":"","content":"I might have gotten the wrong impression for how wide-spread or regular the use of armored bears was supposed to be.<br /> <br /> I thought it was being implied that the bears were domesticated, as opposed to the far greater effort and rarity of taming a wild predator.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T07:18:23-08:00","id":1284129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283839-water-bears-riding-bugs-and-forge-goddesses-new-hundred-devils?p=1284063#post1284063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One could argue that the benthic knifetooth and other purely water-breathing creatures only have the 0-dot version of the Gills merit</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't look at merits designed for human characters when looking at animals. Birds don't have the Wings merit, they're just understood to have wings, just as they lack a Flaw to represent a lack of hands and opposable thumbs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T07:54:57-08:00","id":1284136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283839-water-bears-riding-bugs-and-forge-goddesses-new-hundred-devils?p=1284068#post1284068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But it doesn't explicitly say they breath both in and out of water, it says &quot;Gills in their necks allow them to dive for long periods to hunt fish that live in caves deep below the water\u2019s surface, or to evade human hunters\u2019 spears and harpoons,&quot; which reads to me like they do need to surface like whales.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gills are a physical structure that allow a creature to extract oxygen from water. If the bears were like whales, and needed to surface periodically, I'd expect the description to talk about their ability to hold their breath for long periods instead. The bears can have the ability to breathe underwater indefinitely without the desire to live there permanently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T09:50:55-08:00","id":1284152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283839-water-bears-riding-bugs-and-forge-goddesses-new-hundred-devils?p=1284136#post1284136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Gills are a physical structure that allow a creature to extract oxygen from water. If the bears were like whales, and needed to surface periodically, I'd expect the description to talk about their ability to hold their breath for long periods instead. The bears can have the ability to breathe underwater indefinitely without the desire to live there permanently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because looking at things in the entirely basic l magic based setting of Exalted solely in relation to real world physics, biology, and chemistry has certainly never led to any problems in the past \ud83d\ude09 *coughfiredustcough*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T10:34:36-08:00","id":1284161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283839-water-bears-riding-bugs-and-forge-goddesses-new-hundred-devils?p=1284152#post1284152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, because looking at things in the entirely basic l magic based setting of Exalted solely in relation to real world physics, biology, and chemistry has certainly never led to any problems in the past \ud83d\ude09 *coughfiredustcough*</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This isn't really a question of &quot;biological plausibility&quot;, though. This is a question of &quot;what do words mean?&quot;. If the authors wrote &quot;gills&quot; but intended it to mean &quot;able to hold their breath for a long time&quot;, that's just bad writing, because &quot;gills&quot; has a widely accepted meaning, and if you don't specify otherwise, that's what people are going to assume. If I write &quot;this bird flies using its wings from tree to tree&quot;, it would be a failure of communication on my part if I actually <i>meant</i> &quot;this mammal glides from tree to tree on flaps of skin, and can't gain altitude, just stay level or go downwards&quot;. &quot;It's magic!&quot; doesn't explain <i>poorer</i> capability from things we know exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T11:39:35-08:00","id":1284179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283839-water-bears-riding-bugs-and-forge-goddesses-new-hundred-devils?p=1284127#post1284127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might have gotten the wrong impression for how wide-spread or regular the use of armored bears was supposed to be.<br /> <br /> I thought it was being implied that the bears were domesticated, as opposed to the far greater effort and rarity of taming a wild predator.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that in a case such as this, rarity is relative. If every member of a community that only consists of a few thousand people trains falcons to assist in hunting, as a matter of tradition and even livelihood, it's rare in the overall scheme of things, but still pervasive to that society.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if every member of the tribes that worship the proper avatar are expected to tame a bear, but it might still be enough to be a major factor in their own society, and significant to their interactions with others. That armour doesn't need to be mass produced to be a consideration.<br /> <br /> It might be time consuming, but societies like that can often have time to spare. Even more so if your regular hunting can be assisted by an apex predator.<br /> <br /> Think about it; you kill one Ursid, composed of enough meat to feed your family for a month, that's a month you can spare to taming another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T05:32:05-08:00","id":1284692,"title":"","content":"I'd probably have just a handful of characters in the tribe actually riding them (as oppose to a battle group) but grouping them together like shock cavalry so that the poor bastard they dogpile on gets a sense of what the Tepet Legions went through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T05:40:21-08:00","id":1284693,"title":"","content":"Presumably they're a species of polar bear that got a bit too close to the wyld one time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T12:05:43-08:00","id":1284784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283839-water-bears-riding-bugs-and-forge-goddesses-new-hundred-devils?p=1283848#post1283848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aww man, when I seen water bears I thought it was going to be giant Tardigrades.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I clicked just to see if that is what they did. But hey I love polar bears too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}